dzn: Require attachment support for input attachment usage

vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties accepted
VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT for every format the shaders can load,
block-compressed and packed formats included, which cannot be attachments;
an app that relied on the answer then failed to create the image or view.
Input attachment usage now also needs render target or depth-stencil
support.

From Oliver Bestmann's commit 4f55ccd in github.com/weaselway/mesa (MIT),
where dEQP-VK.api.info.unsupported_image_usage.* passes.

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
index 2af9b67..4b7bcc2 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_device.c
@@ -1712,8 +1712,12 @@ dzn_physical_device_get_image_format_properties(struct dzn_physical_device *pdev
        !(dfmt_info.Support1 & D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_SHADER_LOAD))
       return VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED;
 
+   /* Input attachments also need color or depth-stencil attachment support. */
    if ((usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_INPUT_ATTACHMENT_BIT) &&
-       (!(dfmt_info.Support1 & D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_SHADER_LOAD) || is_bgra4))
+       (!(dfmt_info.Support1 & D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_SHADER_LOAD) ||
+        !(dfmt_info.Support1 & (D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_RENDER_TARGET |
+                                D3D12_FORMAT_SUPPORT1_DEPTH_STENCIL)) ||
+        is_bgra4))
       return VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED;
 
    if ((usage & VK_IMAGE_USAGE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT) &&
